<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yar Muhammad Khan Alakozai</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1851">1851</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yar Muhammad Khan Alakozai was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamran-shah-durrani">Kamran Shah Durrani</a>, ruler of the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herat">Herat</a>. He defended Herat during the Persian siege of 1837–1838, became the real power in the state, and in 1842 killed Kamran, ruling Herat himself until his death in 1851.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yar-muhammad-khan-alakozai.jpg" alt="Yar Muhammad Khan Alakozai" width="320" height="461" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yar_Mohammad_Khan_Alakozai.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
